  "notes": "Cash basis county. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); beginning/ending cash = fund balances 11,296,215 / 11,283,359; transfers in and out 2,791,645 each. Taxes 9,857,065 split by fund-name evidence: Inheritance Fund 728,997 inheritance tax, Visitor Promotion Fund 225,090 lodging tax (p10); General Fund 8,861,638 and 911 Emergency Management 41,340 stay unlabeled (no tax-type breakdown in the trimmed PDF; 911 surcharge not established). The nonmajor statement column's Taxes 266,430 excludes the 911 Wireless Service Fund taxes 52,955, which p4 reports as Intergovernmental. Balance sheet: governmental funds statement of cash basis assets and fund balances (p3, Total column), whose totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (pp5-6, departments not itemized; the budget departments include capital outlay that p4 shows separately), major fund budget schedules (pp7-8), nonmajor combining statement Total column (pp10-13; 16 funds, so fund = Nonmajor funds (combined)); the nonmajor budgetary comparison schedule (p9) covers the same money and is not recorded. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
